_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$f : (X, \\mathcal{O}_X) \\to (Y, \\mathcal{O}_Y)$", "MATH_0005": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$f^\\sharp : \\mathcal{O}_Y \\to \\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0008": "$f^\\sharp$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y \\to f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sheaves-section-ringed-spaces}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sheaves-definition-f-map}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sheaves-lemma-f-map}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1d3a2643500d1263a82ae0a2120a6e4f9d0e6be6a1c713139a53d01d312d5c65", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9f447a75b84af36bbaf9d42376e2981cc780a24a26fa9fa856238075879ba5ab", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that we defined ringed spaces\nin Sheaves, Section <REF_0001>.\nBriefly, a ringed space is a pair <MATH_0001> consisting\nof a topological space <MATH_0002> and a sheaf of rings <MATH_0003>.\nA morphism of ringed spaces <MATH_0004>\nis given by a continuous map <MATH_0005> and an <MATH_0006>-map of sheaves\nof rings <MATH_0007>. You can\nthink of <MATH_0008> as a map <MATH_0009>, see\nSheaves, Definition <REF_0002> and\nLemma <REF_0003>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:55b58b411f23ea2b538a008748b8438a38b2d1e37473aeb452ec7c6beab5ad9f", "unit_id": "inventory:schemes:01HA:paragraph/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:258bb8e215cd7628e5d6b0565e40a23422b1ccfe9f88427750c69eeecd2a3def", "hash": "sha256:258bb8e215cd7628e5d6b0565e40a23422b1ccfe9f88427750c69eeecd2a3def", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 4077, "byte_start": 3163, "file": "schemes.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:f70548ce260f02df0c12473bf504b2650d675f209d9b4d8c8287f1ad1f8a6cc8", "line_end": 112, "line_start": 92}, "owner_tag": "01HB", "parent_tag": "01HA", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01HA", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{definition-locally-ringed-space}", "MATH_0001": "$(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathfrak{m}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathfrak{m}_x$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0011": "$X$", "MATH_0012": "$x$", "MATH_0013": "$\\kappa(x) = \\mathcal{O}_{X, x}/\\mathfrak{m}_x$", "MATH_0014": "$(f, f^\\sharp) : (X, \\mathcal{O}_X) \\to (Y, \\mathcal{O}_Y)$", "MATH_0015": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)} \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{definition}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{definition}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0004": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0004": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f1c6bcec5eb91a37928e969d7bfff99809eff942dad608959ca00a2de9c05c59", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:86acf4a055e829480794e7fe51646eaef0ce7065e9346ce4862d623da5252c1e", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLocally ringed spaces.\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>locally ringed space <MATH_0001><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis a pair consisting of a\ntopological space <MATH_0002> and a sheaf of rings <MATH_0003> all of whose stalks\nare local rings.\n<STRUCT_0004> Given a locally ringed space <MATH_0004> we say that\n<MATH_0005> is the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>local ring of <MATH_0006> at <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>.\nWe denote <MATH_0008> or simply <MATH_0009>\nthe maximal ideal of <MATH_0010>. Moreover, the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0003>residue field of <MATH_0011> at <MATH_0012><TEXTITCLOSE_0003> is the residue field\n<MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0005> A <TEXTITOPEN_0004>morphism of locally ringed spaces<TEXTITCLOSE_0004>\n<MATH_0014>\nis a morphism of ringed spaces such that for all <MATH_0015>\nthe induced ring map <MATH_0016> is a\nlocal ring map.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<STRUCT_0007>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cad5de98a5120cd715a18a56caf03ef8b945c52f146adf9a8cf11173410e2212", "unit_id": "inventory:schemes:01HB:definition/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:c360d09350336a52f4e7e7f4d543d922c29807fb811ab3e5f082c059a9143ced", "hash": "sha256:c360d09350336a52f4e7e7f4d543d922c29807fb811ab3e5f082c059a9143ced", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 3161, "byte_start": 2250, "file": "schemes.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:5b280581f2ea33a4d5d2d5b8d3943e3ab0468de004e4e17a8b676d6e25e08425", "line_end": 90, "line_start": 74}, "owner_tag": "01HA", "parent_tag": "01HA", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01HA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "MATH_0006": "$f^\\sharp$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-section-spectrum-ring}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2cbbdefcd0d7f5f86c1377a8e4f05591c3276893ac18a666a10b1bb5c9a6036b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a24970e28696a9b3da2b4eebaac691f4a3ac689de9978ff5989497f9ae836cb6", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nIn algebraic geometry we study schemes. On a scheme the sheaf of rings\nis not determined by an intrinsic property of the space.\nThe spectrum of a ring <MATH_0001>\n(see Algebra, Section <REF_0001>) endowed\nwith a sheaf of rings constructed out of <MATH_0002> (see below),\nwill be our basic building block. It will turn out that\nthe stalks of <MATH_0003> on <MATH_0004> are the local\nrings of <MATH_0005> at its primes. There are two reasons to introduce\nlocally ringed spaces in this setting: (1) There is in general\nno mechanism that assigns to a continuous map of spectra a\nmap of the corresponding rings. This is why we add as an extra datum\nthe map <MATH_0006>. (2) If we consider morphisms\nof these spectra in the category of ringed spaces, then the\nmaps on stalks may not be local homomorphisms. Since our\ngeometric intuition says it should we introduce locally ringed spaces\nas follows.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:913eb62541bd4a926a6f38217d21f091b494e60b157b33af5c282dddd491bb10", "unit_id": "inventory:schemes:01HA:paragraph/0003"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:ca19d22120c3dbc4364becee8a40c3a6f407bfd07922a5e4301625ee338114c8", "hash": "sha256:ca19d22120c3dbc4364becee8a40c3a6f407bfd07922a5e4301625ee338114c8", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 5217, "byte_start": 4079, "file": "schemes.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:6ec7ee033e5c665ae44bee43eaabbe08429c4443b7df87067ef74c1e7ba3031a", "line_end": 137, "line_start": 114}, "owner_tag": "01HA", "parent_tag": "01HA", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01HA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathfrak{m}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathfrak{m}_x$", "MATH_0009": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0010": "$f : X\\to Y$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$f$", "MATH_0013": "$f^\\sharp$", "MATH_0014": "$f$", "MATH_0015": "$x\\in X$", "MATH_0016": "$$\nf^\\sharp_x : \\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{O}_{X, x}\n$$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathfrak m_{Y, f(x)}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathfrak m_{X, x}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2e54cd990ef5baa3dbbb362a984f35771885c8fe8e449e558622e03690b67cc4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:082608afb4368060b2f58c48c4ce27542908ebbe2774112447e963c4149791e5", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will usually suppress the sheaf of rings <MATH_0001>\nin the notation when discussing locally ringed spaces. We will\nsimply refer to ``the locally ringed space <MATH_0002>''.\nWe will by abuse of notation think of <MATH_0003> also as\nthe underlying topological space. Finally we will denote\nthe corresponding sheaf of rings\n<MATH_0004> as the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>structure sheaf of <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\nIn addition, it is customary to denote the maximal ideal\nof the local ring <MATH_0006> by\n<MATH_0007> or simply <MATH_0008>.\nWe will say ``let <MATH_0009> be a morphism of locally ringed\nspaces'' thereby suppressing the structure sheaves even further.\nIn this case, we will by abuse of notation think of <MATH_0010>\nalso as the underlying continuous map of topological spaces.\nThe <MATH_0011>-map corresponding to <MATH_0012> will customarily\nbe denoted <MATH_0013>. The condition that <MATH_0014> is a morphism\nof locally ringed spaces can then be expressed by saying that\nfor every <MATH_0015> the map on stalks\n<MATH_0016>\nmaps the maximal ideal <MATH_0017> into\n<MATH_0018>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2e86a2626a90993287a1104270bf706e6c9254fde09e2796c219010372c5370f", "unit_id": "inventory:schemes:01HA:paragraph/0004"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:d96a9084587a3002a89284b8db2160495d894b7ccedd6dd9c22fbf1cca644bb6", "hash": "sha256:d96a9084587a3002a89284b8db2160495d894b7ccedd6dd9c22fbf1cca644bb6", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 99138, "byte_start": 99076, "file": "algebra.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:4881df42a56517c183389260487d09d10dab399a86cde2c217f243696240febb", "line_end": 2965, "line_start": 2964}, "owner_tag": "00DY", "parent_tag": "00DY", "requested_label": "algebra-section-spectrum-ring", "requested_tag": "00DY", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "algebra", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "00DY", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{section-spectrum-ring}", "TEXTCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTOPEN_0001": "\\section{"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bdc5ddbdc7f417229ee9bee3df6637a57a3f89cad835eb216e6f6a3e9155cb84", "source_text": "<TEXTOPEN_0001>The spectrum of a ring<TEXTCLOSE_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6baadc7b408a5783f1f23ecffa84160bc332b31dd4bfc0b4649df9ec4d895987", "unit_id": "inventory:algebra:00DY:section_title/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:87709e1b7f262e8a43c8375245122fb09ce189e23b1b87b92c5af3fd373e4403", "hash": "sha256:87709e1b7f262e8a43c8375245122fb09ce189e23b1b87b92c5af3fd373e4403", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 75326, "byte_start": 74690, "file": "sheaves.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:ce890501eac337b11aaa080fa6308548ad9dcf67acba0783ed7129883eba0bc2", "line_end": 2241, "line_start": 2223}, "owner_tag": "008J", "parent_tag": "008C", "requested_label": "sheaves-definition-f-map", "requested_tag": "008J", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "008C", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{definition-f-map}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$\\xi : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\xi_V : \\mathcal{G}(V) \\to \\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}(V))$", "MATH_0009": "$V \\subset Y$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{G}(V) \\ar[r]_{\\xi_V} \\ar[d]_{\\text{restriction of }\\mathcal{G}} &\n\\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V) \\ar[d]^{\\text{restriction of }\\mathcal{F}} \\\\\n\\mathcal{G}(V') \\ar[r]^{\\xi_{V'}} &\n\\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V')\n}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$V' \\subset V \\subset Y$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{definition}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{definition}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8282ad7500c3c7e617ab1c7302ce8bab1307b6baa5a3adffdd4012dfbe8f8ccb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e00ebadca538f087676038c5b6b2c9840c0d246e2b13bf40e1e66a55ceb4f0f7", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a continuous map.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of sets on <MATH_0003> and\nlet <MATH_0004> be a sheaf of sets on <MATH_0005>.\nAn <TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0006>-map <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis a collection of maps\n<MATH_0008>\nindexed by open subsets <MATH_0009> such that\n<MATH_0010>\ncommutes for all <MATH_0011> open.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a902d2e67a9cb925dd92c55f650ed879bef38491a1360667703a8808b84a3bc6", "unit_id": "inventory:sheaves:008J:definition/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:8dfbdb6f7110dc9cab8f26a6a99f99492b7631d89f6e510be76d5935d034fe2e", "hash": "sha256:8dfbdb6f7110dc9cab8f26a6a99f99492b7631d89f6e510be76d5935d034fe2e", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "locat